---
source: crates/broza-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: help_for(args)
---
Detect cleanable categories and estimate reclaimable space

Usage: broza suggest [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --category <ID>
          Restrict to specific categories. Repeatable or comma-separated

      --risk <LEVEL>
          Filter by risk level

          Possible values:
          - green: Only green findings
          - amber: Only amber findings
          - red:   Only red findings
          - all:   No filtering
          
          [default: all]

      --min-size <SIZE>
          Omit findings smaller than this size
          
          [default: 50MB]

      --unused-after <DURATION>
          "Unused app" threshold (for example 6m, 1y, 2y)
          
          [default: 1y]

      --explain
          Include the reasoning behind each detection

      --json
          JSON output on stdout. Disables color, progress and interactivity

      --csv
          Flat CSV output on stdout. Only on tabular commands

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write output to a file instead of stdout

      --no-color
          Disable ANSI color. Automatic without a TTY or with `NO_COLOR` set

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only. Silences progress and non-critical warnings

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostic detail on stderr. Repeatable

      --config <FILE>
          Alternative configuration file [default: ~/.config/broza/config.toml]

      --profile <NAME>
          Configuration profile to apply

      --no-cache
          Ignore the scan cache and force a full analysis

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
